    "analysis": "DocuSeal is a self-hosted, open-source alternative to DocuSign for creating, filling, and digitally signing PDF documents. It provides a WYSIWYG form builder with 12 field types, multi-submitter workflows, email notifications, and a REST API/webhooks, built on Ruby on Rails with a Vue frontend and Hotwired Turbo. It targets businesses and developers who want to self-host e-signature workflows or embed signing forms into their own products, with paid \"Pro\" tiers for white-labeling, SSO, and bulk sending on top of the free core.",
